      "side": 1,
      "message": "So an issue with placing zasserts in helper functions is that we don\u0027t have stack trace to the assertion. So if one were to in the future write a test that calls this function twice, it\u0027d be impossible to know exactly where the test failure was.\n\nHere I\u0027d suggest either:\n\n1) returning a nonzero value in case of failure.\n2) (preferred) Adding an int line parameter that then gets used in the assertion failure message.\n\n2 Example:\n\ncaller:\n`do_fake_sysjump(__LINE__)`;\n\ncallee:\n```\nzassert_equal(system_get_image_copy(), target_image, \"Caller-Line:%u\", line);\n```\n\nThe right solution would be to have a proper stack-trace. This was investigated but not sure what came of it. But I\u0027ll ask the team about it again.",
      "revId": "ba7364fed4a5d7583b5f7f0279dc2d4762653c49",
